    "collapsible_content_Umm6iB": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_eH9W6n": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is MoonShade waterproof?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>We don’t “waterproof” our fabric because it would degrade the integrity of its UV resistance over time. That said, it is seam-sealed and the fabric is very a technical 420 ripstop fabric that will shed water like an umbrella.<br/></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_Ec3Faa": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What is the packed weight of MoonShade Original (9ft x 7ft)?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Not including anchors, a packed MoonShade (9ft x 7ft) weighs about 8lbs.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_cHWALj": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What is the packed weight of MoonShade XL (12ft x 9ft)?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Not including anchors, a packed MoonShade XL (12ft x 9ft) weighs about 12.6lbs.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_QHbtpD": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What is the maximum height of MoonShade/poles?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>The front upright support poles are adjustable and extend to a maximum height of ~ 8 ft. MoonShade can certainly be mounted higher than this, it will simply tilt downward.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_xNbREU": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Does MoonShade also work in the rain?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes! While MoonShade is not technically “waterproof,” it will shed rain in much the same way as an umbrella does. That is, there isn’t a waterproof membrane or coating and the seams are unsealed, but the 420D ripstop polyester fabric is water-resistant and will shed rainwater off the sides and away from what’s beneath it.</p><p>In our manufacturing process, we’ve opted not to use chemical waterproofing treatments or polyurethane/DWR coatings. This was done for two reasons: First, these coatings decrease the service life of the fabric, so MoonShade should enjoy a much longer life in the sun without the added coatings. And second, many of these coatings are very harmful to the environment. While there are no special waterproofing treatments, polyester fabrics by nature absorb less water and dry faster than their nylon counterparts. The domed shape also helps to shed water more efficiently, where flat awnings often sag as water puddles on their surface.</p><p>MoonShade's seams can be sealed to improve wet weather performance using the instructions <a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0549/2637/7049/files/MoonShade_Seam_Seal_Instructions.pdf?v=1648735039\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. Some users will experience dripping at MoonShade's unsealed seams during sustained or heavy rain.</p><p>Please note that while MoonShade can work well to shield you from light rain and was designed to be durable and strong, no awning is engineered for extreme weather or environments, including thunderstorms or gusty winds. If bad weather moves in, it is safest for you, others, and your equipment to stow your MoonShade until it passes. Don’t forget to dry it out once the sun returns!</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_86tXLV": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why is there a reflective coating on the underside of MoonShade fabric?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>In addition to looking great during the day, the reflective coating reflects and blocks the sun’s rays, keeping you cooler. At night, it evenly reflects the light from your LED lantern (not included). The domed shape of MoonShade keeps more light under MoonShade to illuminate all of your after-dark shenanigans.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
