    "collapsible_content_GAnecJ": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_MbEtYF": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can you let me in on some special setup features?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Of course. In addition to all of the great features we’ve mentioned above, here are some standout features we think are the bee’s knees:</p><p>- A simple cord pull set-up allows you to easily mount MoonShade to high/out-of-reach points.</p><p>- The included strut pole allows you to mount MoonShade to narrow structures or use only one mounting point (for attaching to a tree, for example).</p><p>- In addition to resting on the ground, using two suction cups to replace the rubber feet of the support poles, you can set up an angled attachment of the support poles, affixing the base of the poles to your vehicle with the suction cups. This configuration opens a bit more space under MoonShade.</p><p>All of these are described further below… read on!</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_dA6fgP": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How long does MoonShade take to set up?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>MoonShade is simple and quick to set up, even for one person. With practice, one person can set up MoonShade in about 5 minutes. Your first few set ups will take a bit longer as you figure out the best method for your vehicle, so more like 10 minutes to start. Two people can setup MoonShade even faster!</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_UDT3Q6": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How long does MoonShade XL take to set up?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>We designed MoonShade XL to be easily set up by two people in less than 5 minutes, however it can be setup up by one person in calm weather conditions with a few extra minutes of setup time. If you anchor your MoonShade out of reach (like the roof of a tall van), you don’t have to climb up or get out a ladder—the MoonShade can be anchored from the ground using a simple cord pull, allowing you to connect and disconnect your MoonShade with ease, without your feet ever leaving the ground. With MoonShade XL being 70% bigger than MoonShade (9ft by 7ft) we do not recommend setting it up or breaking it down as one person as it is a risk to the safety of the individual as well as to the MoonShade XL itself. Having a buddy for this will make set up and break down easier, quicker, and safer.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_XPGVCJ": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What anchors are compatible with the MoonShade XL?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Because of the size of MoonShade XL (12ftx9ft), and the need for the anchor points to be either set at 12ft or 9ft, this series will be compatible with larger vehicles and units, like but not limited to RVs, larger Vans (e.g., Sprinters, Transits, + Promasters), Airstreams (e.g., Basecamp), medium and large travel trailers, fifth wheels, and more.</p><p>Please note: XL anchors are sold-separately.<em><br/><br/></em>For securing down the MoonShade XL, folks may choose from any of the following anchor options (semi- & permanent):<em><br/><br/></em>All the awesomeness of the original <a href=\"https://moonfab.com/products/seasucker-4-5-seasucker-suction-cups\" target=\"_blank\">4.5″ SeaSucker</a>, but with a stainless steel D-ring for holding ropes, straps, etc. SeaSucker vacuum cups lend themselves to an almost infinite number of uses (e.g., windows, body panels, smooth fiberglass, etc.). If you need to attach something to a rigid, non-porous surface without drilling any holes, this is the best way to do it. You can choose to simply use <a href=\"https://moonfab.com/products/nite-ize-gear-tie-loopable-twist-tie\" target=\"_blank\">Nite Ize Gear Ties</a> (must have a roof rack or other fixed point at 9ft or 12ft to loop ties on) as a semi permanent anchor.<br/><br/>Our semi-permanent <a href=\"https://moonfab.com/products/adhesive-aluminum-anchor\" target=\"_blank\">Adhesive Aluminum Anchors</a> are popular for their always-ready install and secure performance in light and moderate winds.</p><p>Our <a href=\"https://moonfab.com/products/pad-eye-anchors\" target=\"_blank\">Pad Eye Anchors</a> are the strongest permanent anchoring method that uses a stainless steel pad and eye mounted with 3M VHB adhesive and included self-tapping screws. [These are our top recommendation if you cannot mount directly to the roof rack or existing roof hardware and don’t mind making holes (please always contact the manufacturer of your vehicle before any drilling) in your unit.]</p><p>We also offer <a href=\"https://moonfab.com/products/sprinter-rail-anchors\" target=\"_blank\">Sprinter Rail</a>, <a href=\"https://moonfab.com/products/basecamp-rail-anchors/\" target=\"_blank\">1/2\" (Basecamp) Awning Rail</a>, <a href=\"https://moonfab.com/products/awning-rail-anchors-3-8/\" target=\"_blank\">3/8\" Awning Rail</a> and <a href=\"https://moonfab.com/products/awning-rail-anchors-5-16\" target=\"_blank\">5/16\" Awning Rail</a> anchors in case your unit/vehicle has an awning rail channel (check with your manufacturer for location and sizing) as these are considered permanent anchor options.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_VXtLhk": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How can I attach MoonShade to something that is very high, like the top of my van?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>MoonShade comes with several thin lines of paracord that can be attached to the carabiners to create simple cord pulls that will allow you to clip the carabiners to out-of-reach anchor/mounting points without your feet leaving the ground. Stay tuned for a setup instruction video!</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_jfpbr6": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What is the strut pole for?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>The strut pole is included for use whenever you are mounting the short side of MoonShade (9ft x 7ft) to a structure that is narrower than MoonShade (9ft x 7ft) . In other words, in setups where MoonShade (9ft x 7ft) will actually be longer than what you are attaching it to. It works well for mounting MoonShade (9ft x 7ft) to small vehicles or attaching MoonShade (9ft x 7ft) to structures with a single mounting/anchor point, such as a tree.</p><p>If this applies to your setup situation, you can attach the strut pole by feeding the pole through the webbing loop along the center of the short side of MoonShade (9ft x 7ft) fabric that will be attached to the mounting location, then connect the grommet pins on each end of the pole through the grommets on the corners of MoonShade (9ft x 7ft) fabric.</p><p><em>Please note: The Strut Pole is not included with or compatible with the MoonShade XL.</em></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_kyP6YY": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How can I attach the upright support poles to my vehicle?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>If you have mounted the long side of MoonShade to your vehicle using either fixed anchor points (such as a roof rack or another fixed point on your roof) or another strong, non-suction cup mounting solution, you have a second option for the placement of your upright support poles.</p><p>The first option is to set the poles upright with the base on the ground (standard setup). To do this, simply attach the support poles to the front corners of MoonShade’s fabric by connecting the grommet pins at the top end of the poles through the grommets in the front corners of the fabric. Extend the bottom ends of the poles to the ground and adjust the height as necessary.</p><p>The second option is to use suction cups to affix the poles to the side of your vehicle at a 45° angle, keeping the base of the pole off the ground and opening up a bit more space at the front of MoonShade. To do this, remove the rubber feet on the base of the support poles and replace them with the non-velcro suction cups using the pinholes at the base of the poles to affix the suction cups. Attach the top of the support poles to MoonShade fabric as noted above, then extend the poles back to the vehicle, affixing the suction cups and locking them in place.</p><p>Note that it is not recommended to affix the upright support poles to the vehicle with suction cups if you are already using suction cups for the top anchors of MoonShade.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_W36k94": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "You mention anchors a lot. What exactly are anchors? What can I use for anchors?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>When we refer to anchors in our descriptions, we are referring to what you are using to mount MoonShade. Typically when you set up MoonShade, one side will be mounted (“anchored”) to some sort of structure - a vehicle, fence, tree, etc. - and the other side will be supported by the upright support poles. The points/parts/pieces you are using to mount MoonShade are referred to as “anchors.”</p><p>For the side of MoonShade that is mounted to a structure, you have several options for how you can anchor MoonShade. Depending on your setup situation, you may use fixed/permanent anchors or set up temporary anchors.</p><p>Fixed anchors are things that are already available on or attached to what you are mounting MoonShade to. They may be the structure itself. Some examples would be mounting MoonShade directly to the roof rack of your vehicle or directly to a chain link fence. MoonShade comes with sturdy carabiners attached to each corner, so you will typically be anchoring MoonShade by clipping the carabiners to your anchors. In the case of a chain link fence, you can clip the carabiners directly to the fence. Depending on the bar size and length (or width) of your vehicle’s roof rack, you may also be able to clip/anchor MoonShade directly to the roof rack with the carabiners.</p><p>In many setup situations, fixed anchors are not available. In this case, you can set up temporary anchors. Temporary anchors are accessory parts that you can set up to serve as anchors and then remove when you are finished using MoonShade. We’ve designed MoonShade to be versatile, so there are many temporary anchor options that you can use to set MoonShade up in different locations.</p><p>To assist with set up, we’ve included a set of four heavy-duty suction cups that can be used as anchors in MoonShade Original and Golden Hour orders <em>(MoonShade XL anchors need to be purchased separately).</em> Two of the suction cups have velcro straps, to be used when you are mounting the short side of MoonShade using the strut pole, and two of the suction cups are without velcro straps and can be used when you are mounting the long side of 9ftx7ft MoonShade (see the setup guide <a href=\"https://moonfab.co/setup/\">here</a>).</p><p>The suction cups work best on vehicles with metal surfaces and will suction the best to spaces that are flat and clean. While they will work with most vehicles, due to the shape and materials of some vehicles, suction cups will not necessarily work for every setup. Suction cups also work very well on glass/windows, making them a great solution if you are setting MoonShade up along a storefront window or similar location (we don’t want those Girl Scouts (or their cookies) to melt).</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_xm3wUR": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Does MoonShade mount on the 9ft or 7ft side?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Both! MoonShade is extremely versatile and can be mounted on either its long sides (9ft) or short sides (7ft). As long as anchors or attachment points can be placed at either 9ft or 7ft distance, MoonShade's corner carabiners can attach for simple setup.</p><p>See FAQ <em>What is the strut pole for? </em>if you must place anchor points less than 7ft apart.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_YngUeX": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Does MoonShade XL mount on the 9ft or the 12ft side?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Both! MoonShade XL can be mounted on either of its long sides (12ft) or short sides (9ft). Because of the size of the MoonShade XL (12ftx9ft), and the need for the anchor points to be either set at 12ft or 9ft, this series will be compatible with larger vehicles and units, like but not limited to RVs, larger Vans (e.g., Sprinters, Transits, + Promasters), Airstreams (e.g., Basecamp), medium and large travel trailers, fifth wheels, and more.</p><p><em>Note: The XL is not compatible with the Strut Pole.</em></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
