    "collapsible_content_4JcDdj": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_RTmjWQ": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What makes MoonShade different from other vehicle awnings on the market?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>MoonShade's strength is in the awning itself, not the attachment. Most vehicle awnings are permanently mounted to a roof rack — which means you need the right rack, the right vehicle, and you're committing to one setup. MoonShade uses a range of anchor systems (vacuum, magnet, adhesive, rail, strut) to attach to almost any sturdy structure without drilling or permanent hardware. It weighs 8 lbs, packs down to the size of a yoga mat, and works on a Sprinter, a Jeep, a pickup truck, a fence post, or a friend's rig. You're not locked in.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_3MQJFU": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How does MoonShade compare to roof rack awnings?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Hardmounted awnings are heavy, expensive, and locked to one vehicle. MoonShade weighs 8 lbs (OG) or under 13 lbs (XL), packs into a carry bag, sets up in 5 minutes, and moves between rigs without tools. If you want something permanent, a hardmounted awning works. If you want something that fits every vehicle you own and stores under the back seat, MoonShade is the answer.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_Ef8Ki7": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How does a suction-cup or anchor-based vehicle awning hold up in wind compared to a pole-supported awning?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>In moderate wind, a well-staked MoonShade holds reliably. In sustained high wind, take it down — same as any portable awning. For the most secure attachment, Pad Eye Anchors or Rail Anchors give you the strongest hold. The vacuum anchors are built for vehicle use and have held up in rain and wind for thousands of customers.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_aT4mk8": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What vehicles is MoonShade best suited for?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>MoonShade works best on vehicles with a smooth, flat surface for vacuum mounting or a sturdy structure a Strut Pole can grip. Top setups include full-size vans (Sprinter, Transit, ProMaster), trucks (F-150, Tacoma, Tundra), SUVs (4Runner, Wrangler, Bronco, Outback), and Class A/B/C motorhomes. → See the full <a href=\"/pages/vehicle-compatibility-list\" title=\"Vehicle Compatibility List\">Vehicle Compatibility Guide</a> for a complete list of makes and models.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_P4cc9K": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I use a vehicle awning on a car or crossover, or only on vans and trucks?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes. MoonShade works on cars and crossovers. MoonMount vacuum anchors attach to smooth metal roofs on sedans, hatchbacks, and compact SUVs. The main consideration is roofline length — MoonShade OG needs about 7ft between anchor points. Crossovers like the Honda CR-V, Subaru Outback, and Mazda CX-5 are popular setups.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_RnY4yM": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What surfaces or setups are not ideal for MoonShade?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>A few situations where MoonShade needs a workaround or a specific anchor:</p><ul><li>Textured or non-metal roofs — use Pad Eye or adhesive anchors instead of vacuum</li><li>Fiberglass or plastic surfaces — Pad Eye Anchors with 3M VHB adhesive are best</li><li>Open vehicles with no smooth roof (Jeeps, open trucks) — the Strut Pole handles these</li><li>Rooflines under 7ft — check your vehicle in the <a href=\"/pages/vehicle-compatibility-list\" title=\"Vehicle Compatibility List\">compatibility guide</a> before ordering</li></ul>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_6jCfDi": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What should I look for when buying a vehicle awning for the first time?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Four things: Coverage (9x7ft for solo or couples, 12x9ft for groups); Weight (you're setting it up every trip — 8–13 lbs is manageable); Attachment (does it need a roof rack, or can it mount to your specific vehicle without one?); and Pack size (does it fit in your rig without eating storage you need?).</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_fTR3px": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What should I look for when buying a portable awning for overlanding?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Weight and pack size matter more for overlanding than basecamp camping. Look for ripstop fabric rated for UV and rain, aluminum poles, a vehicle attachment that doesn't require a roof rack, and a pack size that doesn't eat into gear storage. MoonShade OG is 8 lbs and packs to 36 x 6 inches. MoonShade XL covers 12ft x 9ft at under 13 lbs.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_NhyA3P": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How do vehicle awnings attach without a roof rack?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>A few ways depending on your vehicle: vacuum anchors grip smooth metal roofs and side panels; magnetic anchors work on steel roofs; rail anchors slide into Sprinter roof rails, RV keder rails, or Airstream awning rails; Strut Poles mount to roll bars and bed rails on open vehicles; and adhesive anchors bond to fiberglass, wood, or any surface that won't take a vacuum. Moon makes all of these — use the <a href=\"https://moonfab.com/collections/moonanchors\" title=\"https://moonfab.com/collections/moonanchors\">anchor quiz </a>to find the right one for your rig.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
